DESCRIPTION:Weighting: 0%\n\nIndividual/team: Individual\n\nAfter you have 
 read this information\, go to the Personality Test discussion board to ask
  any questions and see what your peers are saying about these tests.\n\n--
 -----------------\nAssignment overview\n-------------------\n\nThis task r
 equires you to complete a 'Strengths Profile Assessment'. \n\nThe 'Streng
 ths profile assessment' will identify your top realised strengths\, unreal
 ised strengths\, learned behaviours\, and weaknesses. By completing the 'S
 trengths profile assessment' you will gain self-awareness and insight into
  your strengths and how to develop these further.\n\nThis assignment suppo
 rts course learning outcomes 2\, 3\, 4 and 5.\n\n------------------\nAssig
 nment details\n------------------\n\nTask\n----\n\nStep 1: Go to the [Stre
 ngths profile] (https://www.skillsdiscovery.com/)\, select the 'Free Start
 er Profile' and create an account and password.\n\nStep 2: Follow the inst
 ructions to complete the Strengths profile assessment.\n\nStep 3: Submit y
 our Strengths profile assessment report through Canvas. Your submission mu
 st be in PDF format. No other file format will be accepted. A cover sheet 
 is not required.\n\nSelect each of the following headings to learn more ab
 out the assignment criteria\, submission details\, the use of Gen-AI and y
 our assessment declaration.\n\n[Marking criteria ] (#)\n------------------
 -----\n\nThere are no grades given for your Strengths profile assessment r
 eport.\n\n[Submission details] (#)\n------------------------\n\nThis assig
 nment will be submitted through Canvas. When you are ready to submit your 
 assignment\, select the 'Start Assignment' button on this page and then sc
 roll down to the 'File Upload' tab\, where you can choose your file.\n\nIf
  your assignment has multiple files\, select 'Add Another File' for each s
 ubsequent file before ticking the 'Agree' check box\, then select 'Submit 
 Assignment'.\n\nPlease note: When you submit your assignment through Canva
 s\, you are also submitting the assignment through Turnitin. Turnitin is a
  text-matching service that compares your work with an international datab
 ase of information sources. You will need to agree to use it.\n\n[Using Ge
 n-AI ] (#)\n-------------------\n\nGenerative Artificial Intelligence\, or
  Gen-AI\, is a technology that is used to generate text\, images\, data\, 
 and videos in response to specific prompts.\n\nCourse Coordinators will le
 t you know where and when it is appropriate to use ChatGPT or other Genera
 tive Artificial Intelligence generation software in assessments. As Gen-AI
  is not allowed in all assessments\, it is important to check the guidelin
 es on the permitted use of software in assessment activities. If you are u
 nsure if you can use Gen-AI in a particular assessment\, please contact yo
 ur Course Coordinator\n\nPlease remember your responsibility to uphold aca
 demic integrity. Submitting work for assessment that is not your own work 
 is considered academic misconduct.\n\nFor more information\, please see [A
 dvice for students on using Generative Artificial Intelligence] (https://w
 ww.auckland.ac.nz/en/students/forms-policies-and-guidelines/student-polici
 es-and-guidelines/academic-integrity-copyright/advice-for-student-on-using
 -generative-ai.html).\n\n[Assignment declaration ] (#)\n------------------
 -----------\n\nUoA Online – Assessment Declaration and Statement of Auth
 orship\n---------------------------------------------------------------\n\
 nBefore submitting your assignment\, please ensure you have completed and 
 understood the University of Auckland [Academic Integrity Course] (https:/
 /www.auckland.ac.nz/en/students/forms-policies-and-guidelines/student-poli
 cies-and-guidelines/academic-integrity-copyright/academic-integrity-course
 .html).\n\nBy submitting my assignment\, I declare that:\n\n* I have read 
 and understood the University's [Student Academic Conduct Statute] (https:
 //www.auckland.ac.nz/en/students/forms-policies-and-guidelines/student-pol
 icies-and-guidelines/academic-integrity-copyright/university-regulations-s
 tatutes-guidelines.html)\, as well as the University regulations\, statute
 s and guidelines on [Academic Integrity] (https://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/st
 udents/forms-policies-and-guidelines/student-policies-and-guidelines/acade
 mic-integrity-copyright.html).\n\n* What I am submitting is an original pi
 ece of work\, and no part has been completed by a person or persons other 
 than myself.\n\n* No part of this work has been copied or paraphrased from
  any other source except where this has been clearly and correctly acknowl
 edged in the body of the assignment and included in the reference list.\n\
 n* I have retained a copy of this assignment in the event of it becoming l
 ost or damaged.\n\nI agree and acknowledge that:\n\n* I have read and unde
 rstood the declaration and statement of authorship above.\n\n* I accept th
 at the use of my University of Auckland account to electronically submit t
 his assignment constitutes my agreement to the UoA Online Assessment Decla
 ration and Statement of Authorship.\n\n* If I do not agree to the UoA Onli
 ne Assessment Declaration in this context\, the assignment will not be val
 id for assessment purposes and will not be included in the aggregate score
  for this course.\n\n* I am aware that it is not acceptable to resubmit th
 e same piece of work (in part or as a whole) for multiple assessments with
 out permission from the Course Coordinator.\n\nFurther information relatin
 g to the penalties for plagiarism\, which range from a formal instance of 
 academic misconduct to cancellation of a student's enrolment at the Univer
 sity\, is contained in the University of Auckland [Statute for Student Dis
 cipline (2013)] (https://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/students/forms-policies-and
 -guidelines/student-policies-and-guidelines/academic-integrity-copyright/u
 niversity-regulations-statutes-guidelines.html).
