CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Word/time limit: N/A\n\nWeighting: 10%\n\nIndividual/team: Team
 \n\nDue dates: 11:59 pm NZT 14 August 2026\n\n \n\n-------------------\nA
 ssignment overview\n-------------------\n\nThis assignment focuses on fost
 ering teamwork\, communication\, and organisational skills. In this assign
 ment\, your team will plan the structure and approach for a professional v
 ideo presentation on a chosen topic related to leadership and professional
  skills. This planning phase ensures your team is well-prepared to collabo
 rate effectively and meet the requirements of [Assignment 2B: Team present
 ation] (https://canvas.auckland.ac.nz/courses/145185/assignments/507040).\
 n\nThis assignment supports course learning outcomes 2\, 3\, 4 and 5.\n\n-
 -----------------\nAssignment details\n------------------\n\nTasks\n-----\
 n\nStep 1: Teams of 9 - 11 will be formed at random.\n\nStep 2: Decide as 
 a team on:\n\n* a topic from the provided list (below) or propose your own
  topic related to leadership\, professional skills\, or personal developme
 nt. Topics must be approved by Week 4.\n\n* a chosen method(s) of communic
 ation (for example\, virtual meetings\, shared documents)\n\n* a schedule 
 for meetings or communications (be as specific as possible)\n\n* limitatio
 ns or obstacles regarding team members' availability\n\n* a shared locatio
 n for storing notes\, drafts\, and other materials.\n\nStep 3: As a team\,
  create a project charter document for your presentation. The key elements
  should include\n\n•    Project Title \n       Clearly state the 
 project name and the goal or message of the presentation.\n•    Projec
 t Objectives\n      Define what the video aims to achieve (e.g.\, educa
 te\, inform\, entertain\, persuade). Include measurable outcomes.\n•   
  Scope\n      Specify what will and won’t be included in the present
 ation.\n      Include format\, length (5 mins max)\, and any other cons
 traints.\n•    Team Roles & Responsibilities & Communication\n     
   Identify each team member and their role (e.g.\, director\, editor\, sc
 riptwriter\, project manager\, etc.).\n       Clarify responsibilities
  and expectations for each role. Create a communication structure with mee
 ting minutes            and times\n\n•    Timeline & Milestones\
 n       Outline key phases: planning\, scripting\, filming\, editing\,
  and final delivery.\n        Include deadlines for each phase and a f
 inal submission date.\n•    Success Criteria\n       Define what s
 uccess looks like (e.g.\, the quality of the final video\, team collaborat
 ion\, meeting the deadline).\n            \n\nThere is no specific 
 pre-defined template for the project charter. The design\, layout and pres
 entation of the form must make it easy for a busy executive to quickly gai
 n an appreciation of all aspects of the project\, and as such\, the design
  and presentation of the document are important communication tools.\n\nSt
 ep 4: Submit your planning document in PDF format.\n\nNote: Only one team 
 member needs to submit. \n\n \n\nExample topics or create your own\n----
 -----------------------------\n\n* Building resilience in professional env
 ironments\n\n* Networking effectively for career growth\n\n* Managing stre
 ss and preventing burnout at work\n\n* The importance of feedback and cont
 inuous improvement\n\n* Navigating remote work and virtual collaboration\n
 \n* Developing a growth mindset for career advancement\n\n* Ethical decisi
 on-making in the workplace\n\n* Adapting to rapid technological changes\n\
 n* Mentorship: being a mentor and a mentee\n\n* Time management\n\n* Creat
 e a professional online profile\n\n* Leadership challenges in a new job\n\
 n* Professional work ethic\n\n* Cultural differences in the workplace\n\n*
  Delivering superior presentations.\n\nSupporting resources\n-------------
 -------\n\n* This assignment draws on the content presented in Modules 1
 –6.\n\n* Adhere to APA 7th referencing.\n\n* Refer to your [Assignment 
 briefcase] (https://canvas.auckland.ac.nz/courses/145185/pages/assignment-
 briefcase-2-2) for general support on researching\, writing and referenci
 ng academic assignments.\n\n* Use the [Quickcite] (https://www.cite.auckla
 nd.ac.nz/2.html) (University of Auckland\, n.d.) tool for assistance with 
 referencing.\n\nSelect each of the following headings to learn more about 
 the assignment criteria\, submission details\, the use of Gen-AI and your 
 assessment declaration.\n\n[Submission details] (#)\n---------------------
 ---\n\nThis assignment will be submitted through Canvas. When you are read
 y to submit your assignment\, select the 'Start Assignment' button on this
  page and then scroll down to the 'File Upload' tab where you can choose y
 our file.\n\nIf your assignment has multiple files\, select 'Add Another F
 ile' for each subsequent file before ticking the 'Agree' check box\, then 
 select 'Submit Assignment'.\n\nPlease note: When you submit your assignmen
 t through Canvas\, you are also submitting the assignment through Turnitin
 . Turnitin is a text-matching service that compares your work with an inte
 rnational database of information sources. You will need to agree to use i
 t.\n\n[Using Gen-AI ] (#)\n-------------------\n\nGenerative Artificial In
 telligence\, or Gen-AI\, is a technology that is used to generate text\, i
 mages\, data\, and videos in response to specific prompts.\n\nCourse Coord
 inators will let you know where and when it is appropriate to use ChatGPT 
 or other Generative Artificial Intelligence generation software in assignm
 ents. As Gen-AI is not allowed in all assignments\, it is important to che
 ck the guidelines on the permitted use of software in assignment activitie
 s. If you are unsure if you can use Gen-AI in a particular assignment plea
 se contact your Course Coordinator\n\nPlease remember your responsibility 
 to uphold academic integrity. Submitting work for assessment that is not y
 our own work is considered academic misconduct.\n\nFor more information\, 
 please see [Advice for students on using Generative Artificial Intelligenc
 e] (https://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/students/forms-policies-and-guidelines/s
 tudent-policies-and-guidelines/academic-integrity-copyright/advice-for-stu
 dent-on-using-generative-ai.html).\n\n[Assignment declaration ] (#)\n-----
 ------------------------\n\nUoA Online – Assessment Declaration and Stat
 ement of Authorship\n-----------------------------------------------------
 ----------\n\nBefore submitting your assignment please ensure you have com
 pleted and understood the University of Auckland [Academic Integrity Cours
 e] (https://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/students/forms-policies-and-guidelines/s
 tudent-policies-and-guidelines/academic-integrity-copyright/academic-integ
 rity-course.html).\n\nBy submitting my assignment\, I declare that:\n\n* I
  have read and understood the University's [Student Academic Conduct Statu
 te] (https://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/students/forms-policies-and-guidelines/
 student-policies-and-guidelines/academic-integrity-copyright/university-re
 gulations-statutes-guidelines.html)\, as well as the University regulation
 s\, statutes and guidelines on [Academic Integrity] (https://www.auckland.
 ac.nz/en/students/forms-policies-and-guidelines/student-policies-and-guide
 lines/academic-integrity-copyright.html).\n\n* What I am submitting is an 
 original piece of work and no part has been completed by a person or perso
 ns other than myself.\n\n* No part of this work has been copied or paraphr
 ased from any other source except where this has been clearly and correctl
 y acknowledged in the body of the assignment and included in the reference
  list.\n\n* I have retained a copy of this assignment in the event of it b
 ecoming lost or damaged.\n\nI agree and acknowledge that:\n\n* I have read
  and understood the declaration and statement of authorship above.\n\n* I 
 accept that the use of my University of Auckland account to electronically
  submit this assignment constitutes my agreement to the UoA Online Assessm
 ent Declaration and Statement of Authorship.\n\n* If I do not agree to the
  UoA Online Assessment Declaration in this context\, the assignment will n
 ot be valid for assessment purposes and will not be included in the aggreg
 ate score for this course.\n\n* I am aware that it is not acceptable to re
 submit the same piece of work (in part or as a whole) for multiple assessm
 ents without permission from the Course Coordinator.\n\nFurther informatio
 n relating to the penalties for plagiarism\, which range from a formal ins
 tance of academic misconduct to cancellation of a student's enrolment at t
 he University\, is contained in the University of Auckland [Statute for St
 udent Discipline (2013)] (https://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/students/forms-pol
 icies-and-guidelines/student-policies-and-guidelines/academic-integrity-co
 pyright/university-regulations-statutes-guidelines.html).
