 pecific pre-defined template for the project charter. The design\, layout 
 and presentation of the form must make it easy for a busy executive to qui
 ckly gain an appreciation of all aspects of the project\, and as such\, th
 e design and presentation of the document are important communication tool
 s.</p>\n<p><strong style="font-family: inherit\; font-size: 1rem\;">Step 4
 : Submit</strong><span style="font-family: inherit\; font-size: 1rem\;"> y
 our planning document in PDF format.</span></p>\n<p><span style="text-deco
 ration: underline\;"><strong><em>Note:</em> Only one team member needs to 
 submit.&nbsp\;</strong></span></p>\n<p>&nbsp\;</p>\n</div>\n<div class="we
 ll" style="background-color: white\;">\n<h3><span style="text-decoration: 
 underline\;"><strong>Example topics or create your own</strong></span></h3
 >\n<ul>\n<li>Building resilience in professional environments</li>\n<li>Ne
 tworking effectively for career growth</li>\n<li>Managing stress and preve
 nting burnout at work</li>\n<li>The importance of feedback and continuous 
 improvement</li>\n<li>Navigating remote work and virtual collaboration</li
 >\n<li>Developing a growth mindset for career advancement</li>\n<li>Ethica
 l decision-making in the workplace</li>\n<li>Adapting to rapid technologic
 al changes</li>\n<li>Mentorship: being a mentor and a mentee</li>\n<li>Tim
 e management</li>\n<li>Create a professional online profile</li>\n<li>Lead
 ership challenges in a new job</li>\n<li>Professional work ethic</li>\n<li
 >Cultural differences in the workplace</li>\n<li>Delivering superior prese
 ntations.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class="well" style="background-color: 
 white\;">\n<h3>Supporting resources</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span>This assignment 
 draws on the content presented in Modules 1–6.</span></li>\n<li><span>Ad
 here to APA 7th referencing.</span></li>\n<li><span>Refer to your&nbsp\;</
 span><a title="Assignment briefcase" href="https://canvas.auckland.ac.nz/c
 ourses/145185/pages/assignment-briefcase-2-2" data-course-type="wikiPages"
  data-published="true" data-api-endpoint="https://canvas.auckland.ac.nz/ap
 i/v1/courses/145185/pages/assignment-briefcase-2-2" data-api-returntype="P
 age">Assignment briefcase</a><span>&nbsp\;for general support on researchi
 ng\, writing and referencing academic assignments.</span></li>\n<li>Use th
 e <a class="inline_disabled" href="https://www.cite.auckland.ac.nz/2.html"
  target="_blank">Quickcite</a> (University of Auckland\, n.d.) tool for as
 sistance with referencing.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Select</s
 trong> each of the following headings to learn more about the assignment c
 riteria\, submission details\, the use of Gen-AI and your assessment decla
 ration.</p>\n<div class="oes-accordion">\n<h4><a href="#">Submission detai
 ls</a></h4>\n<div class="oes-accordion-body">\n<p>This assignment will be 
 submitted through Canvas. When you are ready to submit your assignment\, s
 elect the 'Start Assignment' button on this page and then scroll down to t
 he 'File Upload' tab where you can choose your file.</p>\n<p>If your assig
 nment has multiple files\, select 'Add Another File' for each subsequent f
 ile <strong>before</strong> ticking the 'Agree' check box\, then select 'S
 ubmit Assignment'.</p>\n<p><strong>Please note:</strong> When you submit y
 our assignment through Canvas\, you are also submitting the assignment thr
 ough Turnitin. Turnitin is a text-matching service that compares your work
  with an international database of information sources. You will need to a
 gree to use it.</p>\n</div>\n<h4><a href="#">Using Gen-AI </a></h4>\n<div 
 class="oes-accordion-body">\n<p>Generative Artificial Intelligence\, or Ge
 n-AI\, is a technology that is used to generate text\, images\, data\, and
  videos in response to specific prompts.</p>\n<p>Course Coordinators will 
 let you know where and when it is appropriate to use ChatGPT or other Gene
 rative Artificial Intelligence generation software in assignments. As Gen-
 AI is not allowed in all assignments\, it is important to check the guidel
 ines on the permitted use of software in assignment activities. If you are
  unsure if you can use Gen-AI in a particular assignment please contact yo
 ur Course Coordinator</p>\n<p>Please remember your responsibility to uphol
 d academic integrity. Submitting work for assessment that is not your own 
 work is considered academic misconduct.</p>\n<p>For more information\, ple
 ase see <a class="inline_disabled" href="https://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/stu
 dents/forms-policies-and-guidelines/student-policies-and-guidelines/academ
 ic-integrity-copyright/advice-for-student-on-using-generative-ai.html" tar
 get="_blank">Advice for students on using Generative Artificial Intelligen
 ce</a>.</p>\n</div>\n<h4><a href="#">Assignment declaration </a></h4>\n<di
 v class="oes-accordion-body">\n<h4>UoA Online – Assessment Declaration a
 nd Statement of Authorship</h4>\n<p>Before submitting your assignment plea
 se ensure you have <strong>completed and understood</strong> the Universit
 y of Auckland <a class="inline_disabled" href="https://www.auckland.ac.nz/
 en/students/forms-policies-and-guidelines/student-policies-and-guidelines/
 academic-integrity-copyright/academic-integrity-course.html" target="_blan
 k">Academic Integrity Course</a>.</p>\n<p>By submitting my assignment\, I 
 declare that:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>I have read and understood the University's <
 a class="inline_disabled" href="https://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/students/for
 ms-policies-and-guidelines/student-policies-and-guidelines/academic-integr
 ity-copyright/university-regulations-statutes-guidelines.html" target="_bl
 ank">Student Academic Conduct Statute</a>\, as well as the University regu
 lations\, statutes and guidelines on <a class="inline_disabled" href="http
 s://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/students/forms-policies-and-guidelines/student-p
 olicies-and-guidelines/academic-integrity-copyright.html" target="_blank">
 Academic Integrity</a>.</li>\n<li>What I am submitting is an original piec
 e of work and no part has been completed by a person or persons other than
  myself.</li>\n<li>No part of this work has been copied or paraphrased fro
 m any other source except where this has been clearly and correctly acknow
 ledged in the body of the assignment and included in the reference list.</
 li>\n<li>I have retained a copy of this assignment in the event of it beco
 ming lost or damaged.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>I agree and acknowledge that:</p>\n<
 ul>\n<li>I have read and understood the declaration and statement of autho
 rship above.</li>\n<li>I accept that the use of my University of Auckland 
 account to electronically submit this assignment constitutes my agreement 
 to the UoA Online Assessment Declaration and Statement of Authorship.</li>
 \n<li>If I do not agree to the UoA Online Assessment Declaration in this c
 ontext\, the assignment will not be valid for assessment purposes and will
  not be included in the aggregate score for this course.</li>\n<li>I am aw
 are that it is not acceptable to resubmit the same piece of work (in part 
 or as a whole) for multiple assessments without permission from the Course
  Coordinator.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Further information relating to the penaltie
 s for plagiarism\, which range from a formal instance of academic miscondu
 ct to cancellation of a student's enrolment at the University\, is contain
 ed in the University of Auckland <a class="inline_disabled" href="https://
 www.auckland.ac.nz/en/students/forms-policies-and-guidelines/student-polic
 ies-and-guidelines/academic-integrity-copyright/university-regulations-sta
 tutes-guidelines.html" target="_blank">Statute for Student Discipline (201
 3)</a>.</p>\n</div>\n</div><script src="https://instructure-uploads-apse2.
 s3.ap-southeast-2.amazonaws.com/account_61990000000000001/attachments/1803
 4556/prod-uoa-canvas-mobile-clear.js"></script><script src="https://instru
 cture-uploads-apse2.s3.ap-southeast-2.amazonaws.com/account_61990000000000
 001/attachments/3526954/uoa-mobile.js"></script>
END:VEVENT
