DESCRIPTION:Assessment Weight: 10%\n\n* 4% – Peer review of the presentat
 ion\n\n* 3% – Assessment by the teaching team\n\n* 3% – Presentation s
 lides\n\nType: Group Project (Maximum 4 students per group) / Individual p
 rojects are not available.\n\nPresentation: Week 5 (during lecture/tutoria
 l sessions)\nSlides Due: 23:59:59\, 23 August 2026\nPenalty: Students who 
 do not present will receive 0 marks.\n\n \n\nProject Outline: \n\nTheme:
  Design Robot Characters and Applications\n\nYour group will design a soci
 ally interactive robot for one of the following application domains:\n\n* 
 Healthcare\n\n* Education\n\n* Factory working\n\nThe project should demon
 strate how different robot personalities can influence interactions with u
 sers.\n\n[IMPORTANT] We will do project practical exercises in the lecture
 s (Week 1-4). So come to lecture if you need more information on project.
  \n\n \n\nYour presentation should include the following components:\n\n
 1. Application Design\n\n* Select a target application domain.\n\n* Identi
 fy the target users and their needs.\n\n* Define the project objectives.\n
 \n* Describe the system requirements and relevant background knowledge.\n\
 n2. Robot Character Design\n\nDesign at least three distinct robot charact
 ers\, each with different personalities.\n\nFor each character\, explain:\
 n\n* Personality traits\n\n* Social behaviours and interaction styles\n\n*
  Evidence or rationale for the design (e.g.\, literature\, psychology\, or
  user needs)\n\n3. Use Cases\n\nPresent realistic scenarios showing how di
 fferent robot characters behave in the same application.\n\nDemonstrate:\n
 \n* User interactions\n\n* Differences between characters\n\n* Expected ro
 les and benefits of each character\n\n4. Evaluation Plan\n\nPropose a huma
 n-centred evaluation plan\, including:\n\n* Participants\n\n* Evaluation m
 ethodology\n\n* Metrics or questionnaires\n\n* Expected outcomes\n\n \n\n
 Presentation Requirements\n\n* Presentation duration: 6 minutes + Q&A\n\n*
  Submit your presentation slides after your presentation before the deadli
 ne.\n\nMarking Criteria\n\nYour presentation will be assessed on:\n\n* App
 ropriate selection of the target application\n\n* Clear problem definition
  and project objectives\n\n* Well-designed robot characters with supportin
 g rationale\n\n* Effective use cases and potential business or social impa
 ct\n\n* Feasibility of the proposed evaluation plan\n\n* Overall project p
 lanning\, including:\n\n* Gantt chart (project timeline)\n\n* Team roles a
 nd responsibilities\n\n* Proposed methods and implementation plan\n\n* Pre
 sentation quality and slide design
SEQUENCE:0
