DESCRIPTION:Weighting: 0%\n\nIndividual/team: Individual\n\nAfter you have 
 read this information\, go to the Personality Test discussion board to ask
  any questions and see what your peers are saying about these tests.\n\n--
 -----------------\nAssignment overview\n-------------------\n\nThis assign
 ment requires you to complete the [Five Behaviours questionnaire] (https:/
 /canvas.auckland.ac.nz/courses/145185/files/17888535?wrap=1) (PDF 88.9 KB)
  (used with permission by TM&Company Ltd\, now [Oro Collective] (https://w
 ww.orocollective.space/) 2022).\n\nThe Five Behaviours Questionnaire will 
 identify team cohesiveness. By completing the questionnaire you will gain 
 insight into characteristics required for effective teams.\n\nThis assignm
 ent supports course learning outcomes 2\, 3\, 4 and 5.\n\n----------------
 --\nAssignment details\n------------------\n\nTask\n----\n\nStep 1: Downlo
 ad the [Five Behaviours questionnaire] (https://canvas.auckland.ac.nz/cour
 ses/145185/files/17888535?wrap=1).\n\nStep 2: Consider a previous team exp
 erience you were involved in that was either a high-performing and effecti
 ve team or an ineffective and failing team.\n\nStep 3: Complete the [Five 
 Behaviours questionnaire] (https://canvas.auckland.ac.nz/courses/145185/fi
 les/17888535?wrap=1) using this team experience.\n\nStep 4: Submit your co
 mpleted 'Five Behaviours questionnaire' through Canvas. Your submission ne
 eds to be submitted in PDF format. No other file format will be accepted. 
 You will receive full grade point marks on the submission of your 'Five Be
 haviours questionnaire'.\n\nSelect each of the following headings to learn
  more about the assignment criteria\, submission details\, the use of Gen-
 AI and your assessment declaration.\n\n[Marking criteria ] (#)\n----------
 -------------\n\nThere are no grades given for your Five Behaviours Questi
 onnaire.\n\n[Submission details] (#)\n------------------------\n\nThis ass
 ignment will be submitted through Canvas. When you are ready to submit you
 r assignment\, select the 'Start Assignment' button on this page and then 
 scroll down to the 'File Upload' tab where you can choose your file.\n\nIf
  your assignment has multiple files\, select 'Add Another File' for each s
 ubsequent file before ticking the 'Agree' check box\, then select 'Submit 
 Assignment'.\n\nPlease note: When you submit your assignment through Canva
 s\, you are also submitting the assignment through Turnitin. Turnitin is a
  text-matching service that compares your work with an international datab
 ase of information sources. You will need to agree to use it.\n\n[Using Ge
 n-AI ] (#)\n-------------------\n\nGenerative Artificial Intelligence\, or
  Gen-AI\, is a technology that is used to generate text\, images\, data\, 
 and videos in response to specific prompts.\n\nCourse Coordinators will le
 t you know where and when it is appropriate to use ChatGPT or other Genera
 tive Artificial Intelligence generation software in assessments. As Gen-AI
  is not allowed in all assessments\, it is important to check the guidelin
 es on the permitted use of software in assessment activities. If you are u
 nsure if you can use Gen-AI in a particular assessment\, please contact yo
 ur Course Coordinator\n\nPlease remember your responsibility to uphold aca
 demic integrity. Submitting work for assessment that is not your own work 
 is considered academic misconduct.\n\nFor more information\, please see [A
 dvice for students on using Generative Artificial Intelligence] (https://w
 ww.auckland.ac.nz/en/students/forms-policies-and-guidelines/student-polici
 es-and-guidelines/academic-integrity-copyright/advice-for-student-on-using
 -generative-ai.html).\n\n[Assignment declaration ] (#)\n------------------
 -----------\n\nUoA Online – Assessment Declaration and Statement of Auth
 orship\n---------------------------------------------------------------\n\
 nBefore submitting your assignment please ensure you have completed and un
 derstood the University of Auckland [Academic Integrity Course] (https://w
 ww.auckland.ac.nz/en/students/forms-policies-and-guidelines/student-polici
 es-and-guidelines/academic-integrity-copyright/academic-integrity-course.h
 tml).\n\nBy submitting my assignment\, I declare that:\n\n* I have read an
 d understood the University's [Student Academic Conduct Statute] (https://
 www.auckland.ac.nz/en/students/forms-policies-and-guidelines/student-polic
 ies-and-guidelines/academic-integrity-copyright/university-regulations-sta
 tutes-guidelines.html)\, as well as the University regulations\, statutes 
 and guidelines on [Academic Integrity] (https://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/stud
 ents/forms-policies-and-guidelines/student-policies-and-guidelines/academi
 c-integrity-copyright.html).\n\n* What I am submitting is an original piec
 e of work and no part has been completed by a person or persons other than
  myself.\n\n* No part of this work has been copied or paraphrased from any
  other source except where this has been clearly and correctly acknowledge
 d in the body of the assignment and included in the reference list.\n\n* I
  have retained a copy of this assignment in the event of it becoming lost 
 or damaged.\n\nI agree and acknowledge that:\n\n* I have read and understo
 od the declaration and statement of authorship above.\n\n* I accept that t
 he use of my University of Auckland account to electronically submit this 
 assignment constitutes my agreement to the UoA Online Assessment Declarati
 on and Statement of Authorship.\n\n* If I do not agree to the UoA Online A
 ssessment Declaration in this context\, the assignment will not be valid f
 or assessment purposes and will not be included in the aggregate score for
  this course.\n\n* I am aware that it is not acceptable to resubmit the sa
 me piece of work (in part or as a whole) for multiple assessments without 
 permission from the Course Coordinator.\n\nFurther information relating to
  the penalties for plagiarism\, which range from a formal instance of acad
 emic misconduct to cancellation of a student's enrolment at the University
 \, is contained in the University of Auckland [Statute for Student Discipl
 ine (2013)] (https://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/students/forms-policies-and-gui
 delines/student-policies-and-guidelines/academic-integrity-copyright/unive
 rsity-regulations-statutes-guidelines.html).
