 tive Artificial Intelligence generation software in assessments. As Gen-AI
  is not allowed in all assessments\, it is important to check the guidelin
 es on the permitted use of software in assessment activities. If you are u
 nsure if you can use Gen-AI in a particular assessment\, please contact yo
 ur Course Coordinator</p>\n<p>Please remember your responsibility to uphol
 d academic integrity. Submitting work for assessment that is not your own 
 work is considered academic misconduct.</p>\n<p>For more information\, ple
 ase see <a class="inline_disabled" href="https://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/stu
 dents/forms-policies-and-guidelines/student-policies-and-guidelines/academ
 ic-integrity-copyright/advice-for-student-on-using-generative-ai.html" tar
 get="_blank">Advice for students on using Generative Artificial Intelligen
 ce</a>.</p>\n</div>\n<h4><a href="#">Assignment declaration </a></h4>\n<di
 v class="oes-accordion-body">\n<h4>UoA Online – Assessment Declaration a
 nd Statement of Authorship</h4>\n<p>Before submitting your assignment plea
 se ensure you have <strong>completed and understood</strong> the Universit
 y of Auckland <a class="inline_disabled" href="https://www.auckland.ac.nz/
 en/students/forms-policies-and-guidelines/student-policies-and-guidelines/
 academic-integrity-copyright/academic-integrity-course.html" target="_blan
 k">Academic Integrity Course</a>.</p>\n<p>By submitting my assignment\, I 
 declare that:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>I have read and understood the University's <
 a class="inline_disabled" href="https://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/students/for
 ms-policies-and-guidelines/student-policies-and-guidelines/academic-integr
