UID:event-assignment-507045
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE;VALUE=DATE:20260906
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Weighting: 0%\n\nIndividual/team: Individual\n\nAfter you have 
 read this information\, go to the Personality Test discussion board to ask
  any questions and see what your peers are saying about these tests.\n\n--
 -----------------\nAssignment overview\n-------------------\n\nThis person
 ality report provides you with scores on the 'Big Five' factors of persona
 lity (i.e. traits) based on your survey responses. The goal is to help you
  become better acquainted with yourself and your team members. The Big Fiv
 e are Extraversion\, Emotionality\, Conscientiousness\, Agreeableness\, an
 d Openness (exact labels vary by theorist). These traits are comprised of 
 'facets'\, which are narrow personality variables nestled beneath each Big
  Five trait. The report provides scores on both the narrow personality var
 iables and the overall Big Five score. The Big Five can describe people ac
 cording to the following:\n\n* Extraversion: talkative\, assertive\, energ
 etic\, outgoing\, outspoken\, and sociable.\n\n* Emotionality: emotionally
  stable\, comfortable\, and calm.\n\n* Conscientiousness: organised\, thou
 ghtful\, planful\, efficient\, responsible\, and dependable.\n\n* Agreeabl
 eness: sympathetic\, kind\, appreciative\, trusting\, soft-hearted\, warm\
 , and sensitive.\n\n* Openness: imaginative\, intelligent\, original\, ins
 ightful\, and curious.\n\nThis assignment supports course learning outcome
 s 2\, 3\, 4 and 5.\n\n------------------\nAssignment details\n------------
 ------\n\nTask\n----\n\nStep 1: Go to [ITP metrics] (https://www.itpmetric
 s.com/) (n.d.)\, select 'Sign in' and create a free account. Follow the in
 structions to complete the test.\n\nStep 2: Download the PDF report.\n\nSt
 ep 3: Answer the four personal questions.\n\nStep 4: In your team\, discus
 s the four 'team questions'.\n\nStep 5: Submit your ITP metrics personalit
 y report\, including your answers to the four personal and team questions\
 , through Canvas. Your submission needs to be submitted in PDF format. No 
 other file format will be accepted. A cover sheet is not required. \n
 \nSelect each of the following headings to learn more about the assignment
  criteria\, submission details\, the use of Gen-AI and your assessment dec
 laration.\n\n[Marking criteria ] (#)\n-----------------------\n\nThere are
  no grades given for your ITP metrics personality report.\n\n[Submission d
 etails] (#)\n------------------------\n\nThis assignment will be submitted
  through Canvas. When you are ready to submit your assignment\, select the
  'Start Assignment' button on this page and then scroll down to the 'File 
 Upload' tab where you can choose your file.\n\nIf your assignment has mult
 iple files\, select 'Add Another File' for each subsequent file before tic
 king the 'Agree' check box\, then select 'Submit Assignment'.\n\nPlease no
 te: When you submit your assignment through Canvas\, you are also submitti
 ng the assignment through Turnitin. Turnitin is a text-matching service th
 at compares your work with an international database of information source
 s. You will need to agree to use it.\n\n[Using Gen-AI ] (#)\n-------------
 ------\n\nGenerative Artificial Intelligence\, or Gen-AI\, is a technology
  that is used to generate text\, images\, data\, and videos in response to
  specific prompts.\n\nCourse Coordinators will let you know where and when
  it is appropriate to use ChatGPT or other Generative Artificial Intellige
 nce generation software in assignments. As Gen-AI is not allowed in all as
 signments\, it is important to check the guidelines on the permitted use o
 f software in assignment activities. If you are unsure if you can use Gen-
 AI in a particular assignment please contact your Course Coordinator\n\nPl
 ease remember your responsibility to uphold academic integrity. Submitting
  work for assessment that is not your own work is considered academic misc
 onduct.\n\nFor more information\, please see [Advice for students on using
  Generative Artificial Intelligence] (https://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/studen
 ts/forms-policies-and-guidelines/student-policies-and-guidelines/academic-
 integrity-copyright/advice-for-student-on-using-generative-ai.html).\n\n[A
 ssignment declaration ] (#)\n-----------------------------\n\nUoA Online 
 – Assessment Declaration and Statement of Authorship\n------------------
 ---------------------------------------------\n\nBefore submitting your as
 signment please ensure you have completed and understood the University of
  Auckland [Academic Integrity Course] (https://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/stude
 nts/forms-policies-and-guidelines/student-policies-and-guidelines/academic
 -integrity-copyright/academic-integrity-course.html).\n\nBy submitting my 
 assignment\, I declare that:\n\n* I have read and understood the Universit
 y's [Student Academic Conduct Statute] (https://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/stud
 ents/forms-policies-and-guidelines/student-policies-and-guidelines/academi
 c-integrity-copyright/university-regulations-statutes-guidelines.html)\, a
 s well as the University regulations\, statutes and guidelines on [Academi
 c Integrity] (https://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/students/forms-policies-and-gu
 idelines/student-policies-and-guidelines/academic-integrity-copyright.html
 ).\n\n* What I am submitting is an original piece of work and no part has 
 been completed by a person or persons other than myself.\n\n* No part of t
 his work has been copied or paraphrased from any other source except where
  this has been clearly and correctly acknowledged in the body of the assig
 nment and included in the reference list.\n\n* I have retained a copy of t
 his assignment in the event of it becoming lost or damaged.\n\nI agree and
  acknowledge that:\n\n* I have read and understood the declaration and sta
 tement of authorship above.\n\n* I accept that the use of my University of
  Auckland account to electronically submit this assignment constitutes my 
 agreement to the UoA Online Assessment Declaration and Statement of Author
 ship.\n\n* If I do not agree to the UoA Online Assessment Declaration in t
 his context\, the assignment will not be valid for assessment purposes and
  will not be included in the aggregate score for this course.\n\n* I am aw
 are that it is not acceptable to resubmit the same piece of work (in part 
 or as a whole) for multiple assessments without permission from the Course
  Coordinator.\n\nFurther information relating to the penalties for plagiar
 ism\, which range from a formal instance of academic misconduct to cancell
 ation of a student's enrolment at the University\, is contained in the Uni
 versity of Auckland [Statute for Student Discipline (2013)] (https://www.a
 uckland.ac.nz/en/students/forms-policies-and-guidelines/student-policies-a
 nd-guidelines/academic-integrity-copyright/university-regulations-statutes
 -guidelines.html).
