X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://instructu
 re-uploads-apse2.s3.ap-southeast-2.amazonaws.com/account_61990000000000001
 /attachments/18034557/prod-uoa-canvas-mobile.css"><link rel="stylesheet" h
 ref="https://instructure-uploads-apse2.s3.ap-southeast-2.amazonaws.com/acc
 ount_61990000000000001/attachments/3526955/uoa-mobile.css"><p><strong>Weig
 hting:</strong> 0%</p>\n<p><strong>Individual/team:</strong> Individual</p
 >\n<p>After you have read this information\, go to the <span style="backgr
 ound-color: #fbeeb8\;">Personality Test</span> discussion board to ask any
  questions and see what your peers are saying about these tests.</p>\n<h2>
 Assignment overview</h2>\n<p>This personality report provides you with sco
 res on the 'Big Five' factors of personality (i.e. traits) based on your s
 urvey responses. The goal is to help you become better acquainted with you
 rself and your team members. The Big Five are Extraversion\, Emotionality\
 , Conscientiousness\, Agreeableness\, and Openness (exact labels vary by t
 heorist). These traits are comprised of 'facets'\, which are narrow person
 ality variables nestled beneath each Big Five trait. The report provides s
 cores on both the narrow personality variables and the overall Big Five sc
 ore. The Big Five can describe people according to the following:</p>\n<ul
  style="list-style-type: disc\;">\n<li>Extraversion: talkative\, assertive
 \, energetic\, outgoing\, outspoken\, and sociable.</li>\n<li>Emotionality
 : emotionally stable\, comfortable\, and calm.</li>\n<li>Conscientiousness
 : organised\, thoughtful\, planful\, efficient\, responsible\, and dependa
 ble.</li>\n<li>Agreeableness: sympathetic\, kind\, appreciative\, trusting
 \, soft-hearted\, warm\, and sensitive.</li>\n<li>Openness: imaginative\, 
 intelligent\, original\, insightful\, and curious.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>This as
 signment supports course learning outcomes 2\, 3\, 4 and 5.</p>\n<h2>Assig
 nment details</h2>\n<div class="well" style="background-color: white\;">\n
 <h3>Task</h3>\n<p><strong>Step 1: Go</strong> to <a class="inline_disabled
 " href="https://www.itpmetrics.com/" target="_blank">ITP metrics</a> (n.d.
 )\, select 'Sign in' and create a free account. Follow the instructions to
  complete the test.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2: Download</strong> the PDF repo
 rt.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3: Answer</strong> the four personal questions.</
 p>\n<p><strong>Step 4:</strong> In your team\, <strong>discuss</strong> th
 e four 'team questions'.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 5: Submit</strong> your ITP 
 metrics personality report\, including your answers to the four personal a
 nd team questions\, through Canvas. Your submission needs to be submitted 
 in <strong>PDF format</strong>. No other file format will be accepted. A c
 over sheet is not required.&nbsp\;</p>\n</div>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Selec
 t</strong> each of the following headings to learn more about the assignme
 nt criteria\, submission details\, the use of Gen-AI and your assessment d
 eclaration.</p>\n<div class="oes-accordion">\n<h4><a href="#">Marking crit
 eria </a></h4>\n<div class="oes-accordion-body">\n<p>There are no grades g
 iven for your ITP metrics personality report.</p>\n</div>\n<h4><a href="#"
 >Submission details</a></h4>\n<div class="oes-accordion-body">\n<p>This as
 signment will be submitted through Canvas. When you are ready to submit yo
 ur assignment\, select the 'Start Assignment' button on this page and then
  scroll down to the 'File Upload' tab where you can choose your file.</p>\
 n<p>If your assignment has multiple files\, select 'Add Another File' for 
 each subsequent file <strong>before</strong> ticking the 'Agree' check box
 \, then select 'Submit Assignment'.</p>\n<p><strong>Please note:</strong> 
 When you submit your assignment through Canvas\, you are also submitting t
 he assignment through Turnitin. Turnitin is a text-matching service that c
 ompares your work with an international database of information sources. Y
 ou will need to agree to use it.</p>\n</div>\n<h4><a href="#">Using Gen-AI
  </a></h4>\n<div class="oes-accordion-body">\n<p>Generative Artificial Int
 elligence\, or Gen-AI\, is a technology that is used to generate text\, im
 ages\, data\, and videos in response to specific prompts.</p>\n<p>Course C
 oordinators will let you know where and when it is appropriate to use Chat
 GPT or other Generative Artificial Intelligence generation software in ass
 ignments. As Gen-AI is not allowed in all assignments\, it is important to
  check the guidelines on the permitted use of software in assignment activ
 ities. If you are unsure if you can use Gen-AI in a particular assignment 
 please contact your Course Coordinator</p>\n<p>Please remember your respon
 sibility to uphold academic integrity. Submitting work for assessment that
  is not your own work is considered academic misconduct.</p>\n<p>For more 
 information\, please see <a class="inline_disabled" href="https://www.auck
 land.ac.nz/en/students/forms-policies-and-guidelines/student-policies-and-
 guidelines/academic-integrity-copyright/advice-for-student-on-using-genera
 tive-ai.html" target="_blank">Advice for students on using Generative Arti
 ficial Intelligence</a>.</p>\n</div>\n<h4><a href="#">Assignment declarati
 on </a></h4>\n<div class="oes-accordion-body">\n<h4>UoA Online – Assessm
 ent Declaration and Statement of Authorship</h4>\n<p>Before submitting you
 r assignment please ensure you have <strong>completed and understood</stro
 ng> the University of Auckland <a class="inline_disabled" href="https://ww
 w.auckland.ac.nz/en/students/forms-policies-and-guidelines/student-policie
 s-and-guidelines/academic-integrity-copyright/academic-integrity-course.ht
 ml" target="_blank">Academic Integrity Course</a>.</p>\n<p>By submitting m
 y assignment\, I declare that:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>I have read and understood t
 he University's <a class="inline_disabled" href="https://www.auckland.ac.n
 z/en/students/forms-policies-and-guidelines/student-policies-and-guideline
 s/academic-integrity-copyright/university-regulations-statutes-guidelines.
 html" target="_blank">Student Academic Conduct Statute</a>\, as well as th
 e University regulations\, statutes and guidelines on <a class="inline_dis
 abled" href="https://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/students/forms-policies-and-gui
 delines/student-policies-and-guidelines/academic-integrity-copyright.html"
  target="_blank">Academic Integrity</a>.</li>\n<li>What I am submitting is
  an original piece of work and no part has been completed by a person or p
 ersons other than myself.</li>\n<li>No part of this work has been copied o
 r paraphrased from any other source except where this has been clearly and
  correctly acknowledged in the body of the assignment and included in the 
 reference list.</li>\n<li>I have retained a copy of this assignment in the
  event of it becoming lost or damaged.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>I agree and acknowl
 edge that:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>I have read and understood the declaration and s
 tatement of authorship above.</li>\n<li>I accept that the use of my Univer
 sity of Auckland account to electronically submit this assignment constitu
 tes my agreement to the UoA Online Assessment Declaration and Statement of
  Authorship.</li>\n<li>If I do not agree to the UoA Online Assessment Decl
 aration in this context\, the assignment will not be valid for assessment 
 purposes and will not be included in the aggregate score for this course.<
 /li>\n<li>I am aware that it is not acceptable to resubmit the same piece 
 of work (in part or as a whole) for multiple assessments without permissio
 n from the Course Coordinator.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Further information relatin
 g to the penalties for plagiarism\, which range from a formal instance of 
 academic misconduct to cancellation of a student's enrolment at the Univer
 sity\, is contained in the University of Auckland <a class="inline_disable
 d" href="https://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/students/forms-policies-and-guideli
 nes/student-policies-and-guidelines/academic-integrity-copyright/universit
 y-regulations-statutes-guidelines.html" target="_blank">Statute for Studen
 t Discipline (2013)</a>.</p>\n</div>\n</div><script src="https://instructu
