 ity\, and reactivity.\n\nThis assignment supports course learning outcomes
  2\, 3\, 4 and 5.\n\n------------------\nAssignment details\n-------------
 -----\n\nTask\n----\n\nStep 1: Go to [Leadership Circle: Self-assessment] 
 (https://leadershipcircle.com/free-self-assessment/) and complete the reg
 istration. You must complete the entire survey in one sitting. You cannot 
 log back in if you leave.\n\nStep 2: Review your results. Take some time
  to consider where the centre of gravity of your highest scores sits. Cons
 ider the strongest reactions and what countering creative domains might be
  most affected.\n\nStep 3: Submit your Leadership circle: Self-assessment 
 report through Canvas. Your submission needs to be submitted in PDF format
 . No other file format will be accepted. A cover sheet is not required
 . \n\nSelect each of the following headings to learn more about the assig
 nment criteria\, submission details\, the use of Gen-AI and your assessmen
 t declaration.\n\n[Marking criteria ] (#)\n-----------------------\n\nTher
 e are no grades given for your Leadership circle: Self-assessment report.\
 n\n[Submission details] (#)\n------------------------\n\nThis assignment w
 ill be submitted through Canvas. When you are ready to submit your assignm
 ent\, select the 'Start Assignment' button on this page and then scroll do
 wn to the 'File Upload' tab where you can choose your file.\n\nIf your ass
 ignment has multiple files\, select 'Add Another File' for each subsequent
  file before ticking the 'Agree' check box\, then select 'Submit Assignmen
 t'.\n\nPlease note: When you submit your assignment through Canvas\, you a
 re also submitting the assignment through Turnitin. Turnitin is a text-mat
 ching service that compares your work with an international database of in
 formation sources. You will need to agree to use it.\n\n[Using Gen-AI ] (#
 )\n-------------------\n\nGenerative Artificial Intelligence\, or Gen-AI\,
  is a technology that is used to generate text\, images\, data\, and video
 s in response to specific prompts.\n\nCourse Coordinators will let you kno
 w where and when it is appropriate to use ChatGPT or other Generative Arti
 ficial Intelligence generation software in assessments. As Gen-AI is not a
 llowed in all assessments\, it is important to check the guidelines on the
  permitted use of software in assessment activities. If you are unsure if 
 you can use Gen-AI in a particular assessment please contact your Course C
 oordinator\n\nPlease remember your responsibility to uphold academic integ
 rity. Submitting work for assessment that is not your own work is consider
 ed academic misconduct.\n\nFor more information\, please see [Advice for s
 tudents on using Generative Artificial Intelligence] (https://www.auckland
 .ac.nz/en/students/forms-policies-and-guidelines/student-policies-and-guid
 elines/academic-integrity-copyright/advice-for-student-on-using-generative
 -ai.html).\n\n[Assignment declaration ] (#)\n-----------------------------
 \n\nUoA Online – Assessment Declaration and Statement of Authorship\n---
 ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nBefore sub
 mitting your assignment please ensure you have completed and understood th
 e University of Auckland [Academic Integrity Course] (https://www.auckland
 .ac.nz/en/students/forms-policies-and-guidelines/student-policies-and-guid
 elines/academic-integrity-copyright/academic-integrity-course.html).\n\nBy
  submitting my assignment\, I declare that:\n\n* I have read and understoo
 d the University's [Student Academic Conduct Statute] (https://www.aucklan
 d.ac.nz/en/students/forms-policies-and-guidelines/student-policies-and-gui
 delines/academic-integrity-copyright/university-regulations-statutes-guide
 lines.html)\, as well as the University regulations\, statutes and guideli
 nes on [Academic Integrity] (https://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/students/forms-
 policies-and-guidelines/student-policies-and-guidelines/academic-integrity
 -copyright.html).\n\n* What I am submitting is an original piece of work a
 nd no part has been completed by a person or persons other than myself.\n\
 n* No part of this work has been copied or paraphrased from any other sour
 ce except where this has been clearly and correctly acknowledged in the bo
 dy of the assignment and included in the reference list.\n\n* I have retai
 ned a copy of this assignment in the event of it becoming lost or damaged.
 \n\nI agree and acknowledge that:\n\n* I have read and understood the decl
 aration and statement of authorship above.\n\n* I accept that the use of m
 y University of Auckland account to electronically submit this assignment 
 constitutes my agreement to the UoA Online Assessment Declaration and Stat
 ement of Authorship.\n\n* If I do not agree to the UoA Online Assessment D
 eclaration in this context\, the assignment will not be valid for assessme
 nt purposes and will not be included in the aggregate score for this cours
 e.\n\n* I am aware that it is not acceptable to resubmit the same piece of
  work (in part or as a whole) for multiple assessments without permission 
 from the Course Coordinator.\n\nFurther information relating to the penalt
 ies for plagiarism\, which range from a formal instance of academic miscon
 duct to cancellation of a student's enrolment at the University\, is conta
 ined in the University of Auckland [Statute for Student Discipline (2013)]
