 \, 4 and 5.</p>\n<h2>Assignment details</h2>\n<div class="well" style="bac
 kground-color: white\;">\n<h3>Task</h3>\n<p><strong>Step 1: Check</strong>
  your presentation date. Note the week and ensure you are available during
  that time.</p>\n<p><em>Note:</em> Only one team member needs to submit th
 is.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2: Submit your Video presentation to Canvas on th
 e due date mentioned in the assignment</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Step 3: En
 gage</strong> in a 10-minute Q&amp\;A session.</p>\n<p>Your presentation w
 ill be assessed by both peers and teaching staff\, focusing on content qua
 lity\, clarity\, teamwork\, collaboration\, delivery\, and overall profess
 ionalism. Therefore\, attendance is mandatory for all team presentations b
 y at least <strong>two</strong> other teams. Feedback will be provided in 
 class.</p>\n<h3>Example Topics</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Building resilience through
  AI-assisted tools in professional environments</li>\n<li>Networking effec
 tively in hybrid and digital-first career landscapes</li>\n<li>Managing st
 ress\, preventing burnout\, and promoting workplace wellness</li>\n<li>Lev
 eraging feedback for continuous improvement and personal growth</li>\n<li>
 Mastering virtual collaboration and remote team leadership</li>\n<li>Culti
 vating a growth mindset amid rapid technological disruptions</li>\n<li>Eth
 ical decision-making in AI-driven workplaces</li>\n<li>Adapting to emergin
 g technologies like generative AI and automation</li>\n<li>Mentorship dyna
 mics: Guiding and learning in diverse\, multigenerational teams</li>\n<li>
 Advanced time management strategies for high-performance roles</li>\n<li>C
 rafting a professional online presence with personal branding</li>\n<li>Ov
 ercoming leadership challenges in entry-level and transitional jobs</li>\n
 <li>Fostering a strong professional work ethic in uncertain times</li>\n<l
 i>Navigating cultural and inclusive differences for equitable workplaces</
 li>\n<li>Delivering impactful presentations with data visualization and st
 orytelling</li>\n<li>Developing emotional intelligence for human-centred l
 eadership</li>\n<li>Championing continuous upskilling and lifelong learnin
 g paths</li>\n<li>Building trust and psychological safety in teams</li>\n<
 li>Strategic thinking for sustainable and purpose-driven leadership</li>\n
 <li>Conflict resolution in fast-paced\, collaborative settings</li>\n</ul>
 \n</div>\n<div class="well" style="background-color: white\;">\n<p>&nbsp\;
 </p>\n<p><span style="font-family: inherit\; font-size: 1.5em\;">Supportin
 g resources</span></p>\n<p>This assignment draws on the content presented 
 in Modules 1–6.</p>\n<p>Refer to your&nbsp\;<a title="Assignment briefca
 se" href="https://canvas.auckland.ac.nz/courses/145185/pages/assignment-br
 iefcase-2-2" data-course-type="wikiPages" data-published="true" data-api-e
 ndpoint="https://canvas.auckland.ac.nz/api/v1/courses/145185/pages/assignm
 ent-briefcase-2-2" data-api-returntype="Page">Assignment briefcase</a> for
  general support on researching\, writing and referencing academic assignm
 ents.</p>\n<p>Use the <a class="inline_disabled" href="https://www.cite.au
 ckland.ac.nz/2.html" target="_blank">Quickcite</a> (University of Auckland
 \, n.d.) tool for assistance with referencing.</p>\n</div>\n<hr>\n<p><stro
 ng>Select</strong> each of the following headings to learn more about the 
 assignment criteria\, submission details\, the use of Gen-AI and your asse
 ssment declaration.</p>\n<div class="oes-accordion">\n<h4><a href="#">Mark
 ing criteria </a></h4>\n<div class="oes-accordion-body">\n<ol>\n<li>Conten
 t</li>\n<li>Delivery</li>\n<li>Teamwork</li>\n<li>Effectively answering Q&
 amp\;A.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>&nbsp\;</p>\n</div>\n<h4><a href="#">Submission de
 tails</a></h4>\n<div class="oes-accordion-body">\n<p>This assignment will 
 be submitted through Canvas. When you are ready to submit your assignment\
 , select the 'Start Assignment' button on this page and then scroll down t
 o the 'File Upload' tab\, where you can choose your file.</p>\n<p>If your 
 assignment has multiple files\, select 'Add Another File' for each subsequ
 ent file <strong>before</strong> ticking the 'Agree' check box\, then sele
 ct 'Submit Assignment'.</p>\n<p><strong>Please note:</strong> When you sub
 mit your assignment through Canvas\, you also submit it through Turnitin. 
 Turnitin is a text-matching service that compares your work with an intern
 ational database of information sources. You will need to agree to use it.
 </p>\n</div>\n<h4><a href="#">Using Gen-AI </a></h4>\n<div class="oes-acco
 rdion-body">\n<p>Generative Artificial Intelligence\, or Gen-AI\, is a tec
 hnology used to generate text\, images\, data\, and videos in response to 
 specific prompts.</p>\n<p>Course Coordinators will let you know where and 
 when it is appropriate to use ChatGPT or other Generative Artificial Intel
 ligence generation software in assignments. As Gen-AI is not allowed in al
 l assignments\, it is important to check the guidelines on the permitted u
 se of software in assignment activities. If you are unsure if you can use 
 Gen-AI for a particular assignment\, please contact your course coordinato
 r.</p>\n<p>Please remember your responsibility to uphold academic integrit
 y. Submitting work for assessment that is not your work is considered acad
 emic misconduct.</p>\n<p>For more information\, please see Advice for Stud
 ents on Using Generative Artificial Intelligence.</p>\n</div>\n<h4><a href
 ="#">Assignment declaration </a></h4>\n<div class="oes-accordion-body">\n<
 h4>UoA Online – Assessment Declaration and Statement of Authorship</h4>\
 n<p>Before submitting your assignment\, please ensure you have <strong>com
 pleted and understood</strong> the University of Auckland <a class="inline
 _disabled" href="https://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/students/forms-policies-and
 -guidelines/student-policies-and-guidelines/academic-integrity-copyright/a
 cademic-integrity-course.html" target="_blank">Academic Integrity Course</
 a>.</p>\n<p>By submitting my assignment\, I declare that:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>I
  have read and understood the University's <a class="inline_disabled" href
 ="https://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/students/forms-policies-and-guidelines/stu
 dent-policies-and-guidelines/academic-integrity-copyright/university-regul
 ations-statutes-guidelines.html" target="_blank">Student Academic Conduct 
 Statute</a>\, as well as the University regulations\, statutes and guideli
 nes on <a class="inline_disabled" href="https://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/stud
 ents/forms-policies-and-guidelines/student-policies-and-guidelines/academi
 c-integrity-copyright.html" target="_blank">Academic Integrity</a>.</li>\n
 <li>What I am submitting is an original piece of work\, and no part has be
 en completed by a person or persons other than myself.</li>\n<li>No part o
 f this work has been copied or paraphrased from any other source except wh
 ere this has been clearly and correctly acknowledged in the body of the as
 signment and included in the reference list.</li>\n<li>I have retained a c
 opy of this assignment in the event it becomes lost or damaged.</li>\n</ul
 >\n<p>I agree and acknowledge that:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>I have read and underst
 ood the declaration and statement of authorship above.</li>\n<li>I accept 
 that the use of my University of Auckland account to electronically submit
  this assignment constitutes my agreement to the UoA Online Assessment Dec
 laration and Statement of Authorship.</li>\n<li>If I do not agree to the U
 oA Online Assessment Declaration in this context\, the assignment will not
  be valid for assessment purposes and will not be included in the aggregat
 e score for this course.</li>\n<li>I am aware that it is not acceptable to
  resubmit the same piece of work (in part or as a whole) for multiple asse
 ssments without permission from the Course Coordinator.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Fu
 rther information relating to the penalties for plagiarism\, which range f
 rom a formal instance of academic misconduct to cancellation of a student'
 s enrolment at the University\, is contained in the University of Auckland
  <a class="inline_disabled" href="https://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/students/f
 orms-policies-and-guidelines/student-policies-and-guidelines/academic-inte
 grity-copyright/university-regulations-statutes-guidelines.html" target="_
 blank">Statute for Student Discipline (2013)</a>.</p>\n</div>\n</div><scri
