  1</strong>: </span></span><span style="font-size: 14pt\;"><strong style="
 background-color: white\; font-family: inherit\;">Case Study: “The Talen
 t Trap” at KXZY Systems (15 marks) </strong></span></p>\n<p><strong>Read
  the content mentioned in the PDF (step 1) attached titled “KXZY case st
 udy’ and answer the following questions\, drawn from the case study:</st
 rong></p>\n<p><strong>Q1. Bias Identification and Interactions <em>(3 mark
 s)</em></strong></p>\n<p><strong>What types of interpersonal and systemic 
 biases influenced the promotion decision at KXZY Systems? How did these bi
 ases interact to shape the outcome?</strong></p>\n<p><span>Think carefully
  about the individual biases covered in your lectures (such as affinity bi
 as\, halo effect\, attribution bias\, etc.) and map each bias to specific 
 situations or decisions described in the case. There may be multiple valid
  interpretations\, but aim to provide well-reasoned\, evidence-based expla
 nations. These insights will be crucial for informing how you propose to r
 eshape the promotion process and overall culture.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Q
 2. Cultural and Team Consequences <em>(4&nbsp\; marks)</em></strong></p>\n
 <p><strong>What are the long-term risks of unchecked bias for the organisa
 tion (e.g.\, revenue\, brand\, retention)?</strong></p>\n<p>Consider workl
 oad imbalance\, disengagement\, conflict\, and how trust may have eroded a
 cross teams. Try to reflect on real-world case studies or organisational e
 xamples that provide structural evidence of similar issues. You may refere
 nce well-known models or examples from other companies to support your poi
 nts and demonstrate broader understanding.</p>\n<p><strong>Q3. Rebuilding 
 Trust and Driving Change as a New Leader <em>(8 marks)</em></strong></p>\n
 <p><strong>Imagine you have just been appointed as a new department leader
  at KXZY\, tasked with transforming the culture and rebuilding trust.</str
 ong></p>\n<p><strong>What specific actions would you take\, both interpers
 onal and organisational\, to:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Restore trust within
  and across teams</li>\n<ul>\n<li>Redeployment of the existing team VS cha
 nging their culture organically.</li>\n<li>Consider internal hire VS exter
 nal hire.</li>\n<li>Appointing a person from another department\, such as 
 HR/techno-management.</li>\n<li>Appointing a dedicated Chief People Office
 r for people and culture initiatives overall (if so\, how will their activ
 ities help in overcoming such situations\, and what would their daily work
  look like?)</li>\n<li>We need a well-thought-out out detailed plan</li>\n
 </ul>\n<li>Prevent future bias in promotions.</li>\n<li>Ensure high perfor
 mers feel seen and valued.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Be creative but practical: thin
 k about leadership behaviour\, communication strategy\, policy redesign\, 
 and long-term culture building.</p>\n<p><strong><span style="font-size: 14
 pt\;">Tips to answer the questions provided in a separate document titled 
 <span style="font-size: 18pt\;">==&gt\; </span></span><a class="instructur
 e_file_link instructure_scribd_file inline_disabled" title="Talent trap ca
 se study tips 2026-1.pdf" href="https://canvas.auckland.ac.nz/courses/1451
 85/files/17888557?wrap=1" target="_blank" data-canvas-previewable="false" 
 data-api-endpoint="https://canvas.auckland.ac.nz/api/v1/courses/145185/fil
 es/17888557" data-api-returntype="File"><span style="font-size: 18pt\;">Ta
 lent&nbsp\;Trap Case Study Tips.pdf</span></a></strong></p>\n</div>\n</div
 >\n<div id="oes-panel" class="oes-panel panel-default" data-oes-paneltype=
 "default">\n<div class="panel-body">\n<p><strong><span style="font-size: 1
 4pt\;">Part 2</span>:<span style="font-size: 14pt\;"> Self and Learning Re
 flection (10 marks)</span></strong></p>\n<p>Review and consider all the co
 ncepts\, theories and self-assessments we have explored across the entire 
 course. Your self and learning reflection can take a broad (whole of cours
 e) view\, or you can focus on one or more specific aspects that resonated 
 the most with you and inspired most of your growth as a person and/or prof
 essional.</p>\n<ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Make sure you incorporate SMART goals in yo
 ur reflection (Specific\, Measurable\, Achievable\, Relevant\, and Time-bo
 und)&nbsp\;</li>\n<li>Read the information on self-reflection in&nbsp\;<a 
 title="Module 10: Self-reflection" href="https://canvas.auckland.ac.nz/cou
 rses/145185/modules/420724" data-course-type="modules" data-published="tru
 e" data-api-endpoint="https://canvas.auckland.ac.nz/api/v1/courses/145185/
 modules/420724" data-api-returntype="Module"><span>Module 10: Self-reflect
 ion.</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</ol>\n<p>This is a personal reflection. You 
 have been introduced to concepts and theories about your own functioning a
 nd flourishing\, and that of professional and leadership development. The 
 intent of this self and learning reflection is to reflect beyond your prac
 tical and theoretical learnings and 'stand on the balcony' of self.<br>Use
  of your entire strengths profile report is encouraged. Including the repo
 rt as an appendix to your submission is optional and will&nbsp\;not&nbsp\;
 form part of the word count for this assignment.<br>Use the following prom
 pts to guide your reflection:</p>\n<ol>\n<ul>\n<li>How has your sense-maki
 ng been influenced by the information and new knowledge you are gathering 
 in this course?</li>\n<li>How can&nbsp\;you view or explain past events\, 
 experiences\, challenges\, and adversity in different ways by looking thro
 ugh the lens of new concepts you have been exposed to during this course?<
 /li>\n<li>How is this course influencing\, broadening or shaping your pers
 pectives on the concept of a highly effective and flourishing person and p
 rofessional?</li>\n<li>What core belief(s) did you hold coming into the co
 urse\, and how have these beliefs (s) shifted?</li>\n<li>What key learning
  are you taking away\, and how do you intend to adopt and integrate these 
 in your personal and professional life post this course?</li>\n</ul>\n</ol
 >\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id="oes-panel" class="oes-panel panel-default" dat
 a-oes-paneltype="default">\n<div class="panel-body">\n<p><strong><span sty
 le="font-size: 14pt\;">Supporting Resources</span></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li
 >This assignment draws on the content presented in Modules 1–10.</li>\n<
 li>Refer to your <a title="Assignment briefcase" href="https://canvas.auck
 land.ac.nz/courses/145185/pages/assignment-briefcase-2-2" data-course-type
 ="wikiPages" data-published="true" data-api-endpoint="https://canvas.auckl
 and.ac.nz/api/v1/courses/145185/pages/assignment-briefcase-2-2" data-api-r
 eturntype="Page">Assignment briefcase</a> for general support on researchi
 ng\, writing and referencing academic assignments.</li>\n<li>Use the <a cl
 ass="inline_disabled" href="https://www.cite.auckland.ac.nz/2.html" target
 ="_blank">Quickcite</a> (University of Auckland\, n.d.) tool for assistanc
 e with referencing.</li>\n<li>To assist you with completing this assignmen
 t\, you may wish to refer to <a class="inline_disabled" href="https://www.
 learninghub.ac.nz/writing/reflective-writing/" target="_blank">Reflective 
 writing</a> (University of Auckland\, n.d.) in the University of Auckland 
 Learning Hub.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<h3><a href="#">Assessm
