DESCRIPTION:Participate and Reflect on two Professional Development Worksho
 ps (5%)\n\nSelf learning and reflection: 2x 250 words (+/− 10%)\n\nWeigh
 ting: 5%\n\nIndividual/team: Individual\n\nIf anything about assignment 4 
 is unclear\, post your question on the d[iscussion board.] (https://canvas
 .auckland.ac.nz/courses/145185/discussion_topics/1637603) You can connect 
 with fellow students there\, and a graduate teaching assistant will respon
 d to any unanswered queries.\nFor questions that can’t be resolved on th
 e board or any other issues\, contact Tim Hoksbergen directly at [tim.hoks
 bergen@auckland.ac.nz] (mailto:tim.hoksbergen@auckland.ac.nz)\n\nBrief\n\n
 Identify\, attend\, and actively participate in at least 2 workshops.\nSub
 mit a short learning reflection (approx. 250 words) for each of the worksh
 ops you attended. Quality matters more than quantity!\nSubmit one document
  reflecting on the two workshops. Clearly state the workshops you attended
 .\n\nThe workshop organiser also tracks workshop attendance. Attendance re
 cords are provided to the teaching staff at the end of the semester and re
 viewed as part of the grading process.\n\nYou should select the workshops 
 based on your most important professional development needs.\n\nAttend wor
 kshops you have registered for or provide as much (but at least 24 hours) 
 notice as possible if you can no longer attend due to unforeseen circumsta
 nces.\nDisplaying behaviour expected of a professional and postgraduate-le
 vel student\, including actively participating in the workshop\, treating 
 the facilitator and fellow participants with respect\, and engaging in all
  activities.\nSupport the facilitator in creating an environment that opti
 mises learning for everyone.\n\nThe available workshops given by the Facul
 ty of Engineering are listed on the ENGRAD Canvas page. If you don’t hav
 e access to this page\, you can email Joanna Luo ([joanna.luo@auckland.ac.
 nz] (mailto:joanna.luo@auckland.ac.nz)) and request access to this page.\n
 \n \n\nSupporting resources\n--------------------\n\n* This assignment dr
